{"claims":[{"excerpt":"Webb moest opgevouwen in de Ariane 5-raket passen.","claim":"Webb had to be folded to fit in the Ariane 5 rocket.","category":"technical","label":"F1","evidence":"Webb was designed to fold into a compact launch configuration that fit inside the Ariane 5.","narrative":"Webb moest compact in de Ariane 5-raket passen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source specifies that Webb fit inside the rocket fairing; saying it fit in the rocket is a common shorthand but less technically precise.","materiality":"Minor technical imprecision; it does not change the account of why Webb was folded."},{"excerpt":"In de ruimte moest de telescoop zich daarna stap voor stap ontvouwen","claim":"After launch, Webb had to unfold step by step in space.","category":"chronology","label":"F0","evidence":"In the two weeks after launch, the entire observatory underwent a highly choreographed transformation"; “Deployments began minutes after separation.”","narrative":"De uitvouwing bracht de telescoop in de tweede week in die configuratie","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes a choreographed sequence of deployments beginning shortly after separation and continuing over the following days.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"een ingewikkelde fase met veel mogelijke faalpunten.","claim":"The unfolding was complex and involved many possible points of failure.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"There were over 50 major deployment steps, with 178 release mechanisms that had to perform perfectly or any one of over 300 single points of failure could have diminished or crippled the mission.","narrative":"De uitvouwing omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten, waardoor duidelijk is dat dit een risicovolle fase was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source documents a complex deployment with over 300 possible single points of failure.","materiality":"The claim conveys the documented stakes without implying a failure occurred."},{"excerpt":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgeklapt en vergrendeld.","claim":"By the second week, Webb’s mirror structures had unfolded and latched.","category":"chronology","label":"F0","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings.","narrative":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source reports that the secondary mirror tripod and both primary-mirror wings were unfolded and latched. “Spiegels” is a concise description of these structures.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"Webb had daarmee zijn operationele configuratie bereikt.","claim":"The mirror deployment brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","category":"outcome","label":"F0","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"had Webb zijn operationele configuratie bereikt","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This matches the source’s stated result of the second-week deployment.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing verliep soepel","claim":"Webb’s deployment proceeded smoothly.","category":"outcome","label":"F0","evidence":"Webb's deployment was completed with remarkable smoothness.","narrative":"de uitvouwing verliep soepel","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly characterizes the deployment as remarkably smooth.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"maar dat betekende nog niet dat de telescoop klaar was voor routinewetenschap.","claim":"Reaching the deployed configuration did not mean Webb was ready for routine science.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments."; “After six months: ‘Science operations!’ Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.”","narrative":"maar was niet hetzelfde als klaar zijn voor routinewetenschap","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source distinguishes completion of deployment from the further commissioning needed before routine science operations.","materiality":"This is the central distinction established by the source."},{"excerpt":"Tijdens de ingebruikname bleef Webb wekenlang afkoelen.","claim":"Webb continued cooling for several weeks during commissioning.","category":"chronology","label":"F0","evidence":"The telescope and scientific instruments started to cool rapidly in the shade of the sunshield, but it took several weeks for them to cool all the way down and reach stable temperatures.","narrative":"afkoeling ... liepen door tijdens de ingebruikname van zes maanden","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places several weeks of cooling within the commissioning timeline.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"Daarna volgden maanden van spiegeluitlijning en instrumentkalibratie.","claim":"Mirror alignment and instrument calibration followed the cooling phase over subsequent months.","category":"chronology","label":"F1","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments."; “In the second, third and fourth months: Initial optics checkouts, and telescope alignment.”; “In the fifth and sixth months: Calibration and completion of commissioning.”","narrative":"afkoeling, spiegeluitlijning en instrumentkalibratie liepen door tijdens de ingebruikname van zes maanden","narrativeRelation":"ambiguous","origin":"unknown","explanation":"The source supports the broad progression from initial cooling to alignment and then calibration, but also says cooldown effectively ended during months two through four, when alignment was underway. “Daarna” can suggest a cleaner sequential transition than the source establishes.","materiality":"Minor chronology compression; the source’s main timeline and six-month commissioning period remain intact."},{"excerpt":"Pas na zes maanden begon de routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb began routine science operations after six months.","category":"chronology","label":"F0","evidence":"After six months: ‘Science operations!’ Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The stated timing and outcome match the source.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."},{"excerpt":"Uitgevouwen zijn was dus een belangrijke mijlpaal","claim":"Reaching the deployed configuration was an important milestone.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration."; “The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments.”","narrative":"uitgevouwen zijn een belangrijke mijlpaal was","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The deployment completed a major operational configuration step, while commissioning continued afterward.","materiality":"A supported summary of the source’s timeline."},{"excerpt":"niet het eindpunt van Webbs ingebruikname.","claim":"Deployment was not the endpoint of Webb’s commissioning.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments.","narrative":"niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly describes further commissioning after deployment was complete.","materiality":"No material discrepancy."}]}

